{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":1,"query":"name=Hennessy&limit=10&title=Leading Matters","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":{"title":"Leading matters ","subTitle":"lessons from my journey "},"name":[{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Hennessy, John L.,","role":[{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author"}}]},{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Isaacson, Walter,","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"writer of foreword"}}}],"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"biography"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"text"},{"@authority":"Medical Subject Headings","#text":"Autobiography"},{"@authority":"aat","#text":"autobiographies (literary genre)"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Autobiographies"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Biographies"},{"@authority":"lcgft","#text":"Autobiographies."},{"@authority":"rvmgf","#text":"Autobiographies."}],"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"cau"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"California"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2018"},"copyrightDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2018"},"issuance":"monographic"},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"Stanford, California :"}},"agent":{"namePart":"Stanford Business Books, an imprint of Stanford University Press,","role":{"roleTerm":"publisher"}},"dateIssued":[2018]}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"unmediated"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"volume"}],"extent":"xii, 186 pages ; 24 cm"},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"In Leading Matters, current Chairman of Alphabet (Google's parent company), former President of Stanford University, and \"Godfather of Silicon Valley,\" John L. Hennessy shares the core elements of leadership that helped him become a successful tech entrepreneur, esteemed academic, and venerated administrator. Hennessy's approach to leadership is laser-focused on the journey rather than the destination. Each chapter in Leading Matters looks at valuable elements that have shaped Hennessy's career in practice and philosophy. He discusses the pivotal role that humility, authenticity and trust, service, empathy, courage, collaboration, innovation, intellectual curiosity, storytelling, and legacy have all played in his prolific, interdisciplinary career."},"tableOfContents":{"@type":"Contents","#text":"Humility : the basis for effective leadership -- Authenticity and trust : the essential ingredients for effective leadership -- Leadership as service : understanding who works for whom -- Empathy : how it shapes a leader and an institution -- Courage : standing up for the institution and the community -- Collaboration and teamwork : you cannot do it alone -- Innovation : the key to success in industry and academia -- Intellectual curiosity : why being a lifelong learner is crucial -- Storytelling : communicating a vision -- Legacy : what you leave behind -- Conclusion : building the future."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"John L. Hennessy ; foreword by Walter Isaacson."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references (pages 159-180) and index."},{"@type":"language","#text":"In English."}],"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"n-us---"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Hennessy, John L."}},{"@authority":"fast","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":"Hennessy, John L.","nameIdentifier":"https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJmHChDKTDxVkKCkRR4Dv3"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":